# === Rule: structural positions hold forms, not literals ==================== #

ex:ecSlotFormResource a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/slot-form-resource.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lang:FormSlot whose lang:slotForm points at a lang:Form resource satisfies lang:SlotFormStructuralShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecSlotFormLiteral a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/slot-form-literal.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.NodeKindConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example gives lang:slotForm a bare string literal (sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI on lang:SlotFormStructuralShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.NodeKindConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:StringOnlyForm)." .

# === Rule: graphemes are grounded in their script's repertoire ============== #

ex:ecGraphemeGrounded a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/grapheme-grounded.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lang:Grapheme listed in its lang:Script's repertoire through lang:hasGrapheme satisfies lang:GraphemeGroundedShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecGraphemeUngrounded a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/grapheme-ungrounded.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's lang:Grapheme declares a lang:Script that does not list it through lang:hasGrapheme (the SPARQL constraint of lang:GraphemeGroundedShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UngroundedGrapheme)." .

ex:ecGraphemeNoScript a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/grapheme-no-script.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's lang:Grapheme declares no lang:inScript at all (sh:minCount 1 on lang:GraphemeGroundedShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UngroundedGrapheme)." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Meaning-stratum fixtures — the Frege triangle, the denotation record, the
# one-way logic: bridge, interpretation, ambiguity, deixis, and speech acts.
# lang:SilentDisambiguation and lang:UndeclaredLoweringStage are native Rust gates
# (crates/validate structural_lint) tested in-crate, not SHACL, so they have no
# example-conformance cell here.
# =========================================================================== #

ex:ecMeaningCatsChaseMice a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-cats-chase-mice.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Flagship 1: 'cats chase mice' denotes a logic:Formula through a compositional lowering (lang:composedBy / lang:composedFrom) with a per-stage logic:preservationKind, routed through a sense — satisfies every denotation gate and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecMeaningScopeAmbiguity a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-scope-ambiguity.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Two co-resident readings of one sentence denote two DISTINCT logic:Formulas (forall-exists vs exists-forall); both persist, neither is collapsed, and each carries a preservation judgment." .

ex:ecMeaningSawHerDuck a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-saw-her-duck.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Two co-resident readings via two senses of one lexeme, each routed through lang:viaSense (satisfying lang:AmbiguityRoutingShape); the annotator's preference is a vantage-held gmeow:Observation with logic:confidence, and the other reading persists." .

ex:ecMeaningSenseHypernymy a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-sense-hypernymy.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The senses of 'dog' and 'animal' denote two logic:Types whose hypernymy is carried as logic: subsumption over the denoted types, with a reified lang:SenseRelation recording it — the lattice preserved as logic: linkage." .

ex:ecMeaningHigherOrder a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-higher-order.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A claim about a claim about a reading (three reified vantage-held observations) — the HiLog-reflectable spine supports higher-order reasoning; each reading-claim names its vantage." .

ex:ecMeaningCompetencyQuestion a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-competency-question.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Flagship 2: a competency question's own prose is a lang:SurfaceForm realizing a parsed form; a lang:CommunicativeAct with interrogative force whose content denotes a query (lang:denotesQuery). GMEOW reads its own prose." .

ex:ecMeaningMemoryClaim a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-memory-claim.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Principle 14/15: a stored claim's raw text is lifted to a form, interpreted, and held as a vantage-held reading — the store/recall construct the memory layer consumes." .

ex:ecMeaningIndexicalAnchor a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-indexical-anchor.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "An indexical denotation whose interpretation act names a lang:IndexicalAnchor (person deixis) satisfies lang:IndexicalAnchoredShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecMeaningCoreference a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-coreference.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Two referring expressions introduce and co-refer with one lang:DiscourseReferent — the anaphora primitive — and validate with no findings." .

ex:ecMeaningPresupposition a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-presupposition.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A denotation whose asserted content and lang:presupposes content are two distinct logic:Formulas — separate lowerings — validates with no findings." .

ex:ecMeaningUnderspecifiedDenotation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-underspecified-denotation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The denotation omits lang:denotationContext (sh:minCount 1 on lang:DenotationRecordShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnderspecifiedDenotation)." .

ex:ecMeaningSurfaceDenotation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-surface-denotation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The denotation's lang:denotedForm is a lang:SurfaceForm (the SPARQL constraint of lang:DenotationNonSurfaceShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:SurfaceLevelDenotation)." .

ex:ecMeaningUnroutedAmbiguous a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-unrouted-ambiguous.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The denoted form's head lexeme has two senses but the denotation omits lang:viaSense (the SPARQL constraint of lang:AmbiguityRoutingShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnroutedAmbiguousDenotation)." .

ex:ecMeaningKindMismatch a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-kind-mismatch.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The denotesLogicFormula denotation targets a logic:Type, not a logic:Formula (the SPARQL constraint of lang:DenotationKindMatchShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:DenotationKindMismatch)." .

ex:ecMeaningUngroundedClaim a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-ungrounded-claim.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The observation about a reading names no gmeow:vantage (sh:minCount 1 on lang:ReadingClaimGroundedShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UngroundedReadingClaim)." .

ex:ecMeaningUnanchoredIndexical a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-unanchored-indexical.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The indexical denotation's interpretation act names no lang:IndexicalAnchor (the SPARQL constraint of lang:IndexicalAnchoredShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnanchoredIndexical)." .

ex:ecMeaningConfidenceAsProbability a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-confidence-as-probability.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The reading claim carries a logic:probability with no declared logic:probabilityModel (the SPARQL constraint of lang:ConfidenceNotProbabilityShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:ConfidenceAsProbability)." .

ex:ecMeaningFregeConflation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-frege-conflation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "One node is typed as both lang:Sense and lang:Denotation (the SPARQL constraint of the SECONDARY lang:FregeDisjointShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:FregeConflation)." .

ex:ecMeaningActObservationConflation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/meaning-act-observation-conflation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.NotConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lang:InterpretationAct is typed also as a gmeow:Observation (the sh:not of the SECONDARY lang:ActObservationDisjointShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.NotConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:ActObservationConflation)." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Translation-stratum fixtures — the crossing layer: renderings, transliteration
# maps, translation units carrying a logic:Correspondence, document roll-ups, and
# paraphrase. lang:FabricatedEquivalence, lang:AssertedRollup, lang:SurfaceLeakInContentKey,
# and the PRIMARY lang:RenderingAsIdentity (content and produced form being one node) are
# native Rust gates (crates/validate structural_lint) tested in-crate, not SHACL, so they
# have no example-conformance cell here.
# =========================================================================== #

ex:ecTranslationFrenchEnglishPair a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/translation-french-english-pair.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Flagship translation: an English→French document with two lang:TranslationUnits, each carrying exactly one logic:Correspondence with an honest logic:ValidationOnly judgment, rolled up by a document-level lang:Translation that asserts no document-level preservation — satisfies lang:TranslationUnitShape, lang:UnmarkedSurfaceTranslationShape, and lang:TranslationAttributionShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecTranslationTransliterationISO9 a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/translation-transliteration-iso9.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A round-trippable ISO 9 lang:TransliterationMap (source/target orthography + scheme) whose application is held as a lang:Rendering carrying logic:ExactPreservation satisfies lang:TransliterationAnchorShape and lang:RenderingRecordShape / lang:RenderingNotIdentityShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecTransliterationLossyRomanization a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/transliteration-lossy-romanization.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lossy Arabic romanization lang:TransliterationMap whose rendering carries logic:SoundUnderApproximation — declaring the unrecoverable short-vowel and letter-seat residue as data rather than a silent Exact default — satisfies lang:TransliterationAnchorShape and lang:RenderingRecordShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecParaphraseSameDenotation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/paraphrase-same-denotation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lang:Paraphrase within one English sign system declaring lang:paraphraseSamenessKind lang:sameDenotation satisfies lang:ParaphraseKindShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecRenderingTurtleEmit a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/rendering-turtle-emit.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lang:Rendering of kind lang:renderingSerialization producing a Turtle lang:SurfaceForm distinct from its rendered content, carrying logic:ExactPreservation, satisfies lang:RenderingRecordShape and lang:RenderingNotIdentityShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecRenderingProseGloss a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/rendering-prose-gloss.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lang:Rendering of kind lang:renderingProse glossing a logic:Formula as English prose, carrying logic:SoundUnderApproximation (the gloss loses precise quantifier scope), satisfies lang:RenderingRecordShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecTranslationUntranslatableResidue a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/translation-untranslatable-residue.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A lang:TranslationUnit for the untranslatable Japanese 間 whose carried logic:Correspondence is logic:Unsupported with logic:mnemomorphic false and which is marked lang:translationGap — untranslatability held as data — satisfies lang:TranslationUnitShape, lang:UnmarkedSurfaceTranslationShape (both sides UnanalyzedProse, weakest judgment), and lang:TranslationAttributionShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecRenderingUnderspecified a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/rendering-underspecified.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The lang:Rendering omits its lang:renderedContent (sh:minCount 1 on lang:RenderingRecordShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnderspecifiedRendering); the self-identity SPARQL branch cannot match with no renderedContent." .

ex:ecTranslationUnitUnderspecified a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/translation-unit-underspecified.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The lang:TranslationUnit omits its single lang:translationCorrespondence (sh:minCount 1 on lang:TranslationUnitShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnderspecifiedTranslationUnit); the unmarked-surface SPARQL branch binds through the absent correspondence and cannot match." .

ex:ecTranslationUnmarkedSurface a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/translation-unmarked-surface.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The unit's lang:translationSource is a lang:SurfaceForm that realizes nothing and is not typed lang:UnanalyzedProse while its logic:Correspondence claims logic:ExactPreservation (the sh:sparql constraint of lang:UnmarkedSurfaceTranslationShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnmarkedSurfaceTranslation); the segmented analysis level keeps the surface-analysis gate quiet." .

ex:ecTranslationUnanalyzedOverclaim a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/translation-unanalyzed-overclaim.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "Both surfaces ARE typed lang:UnanalyzedProse (rawLevel, realizing nothing) yet the carried logic:Correspondence claims logic:ExactPreservation — the second conjunct of the honest 'unanalyzed AND weakest-judgment' rule is violated, so the OR-structured sh:sparql constraint of lang:UnmarkedSurfaceTranslationShape MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnmarkedSurfaceTranslation). An AND-structured gate would miss this — an unanalyzed surface may not claim an exact crossing." .

ex:ecTranslationUnattributed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/translation-unattributed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The lang:TranslationUnit declares no lang:translationMethod (sh:minCount 1 on lang:TranslationAttributionShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnattributedTranslation); the machine-attribution SPARQL branch cannot match an absent method." .

ex:ecParaphraseUndeclaredKind a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/paraphrase-undeclared-kind.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
