ex:ecTransliterationUnanchored a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/transliteration-unanchored.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The lang:TransliterationMap declares no lang:transliterationScheme (sh:minCount 1 on lang:TransliterationAnchorShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:UnanchoredTransliteration); both orthographies are declared." .

# === Rule: every projection declares its logic:preservationKind ============= #

ex:ecComposedFormCodeSwitch a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/composed-form-code-switch.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A code-switched lang:ComposedForm (English matrix with an embedded French constituent) whose slots realize word forms in DIFFERENT sign systems, with contiguous zero-based lang:slotIndex and structural lang:slotForm resources, satisfies the slot shapes and lang:FormSituatedShape and validates with NO findings — code-switching is native data, never collapsed to one language." .

ex:ecProjectionOntolexLemonEmission a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/projection-ontolex-lemon-emission.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A well-formed lang:ProjectionEmission (the OntoLex-Lemon lowering of a lang:Lexeme) declares its lang:projectionTargetName and logic:preservationKind (logic:SoundUnderApproximation) and enumerates every flattened epistemic stratum as lang:unsupportedConstruct, so it satisfies lang:ProjectionEmissionDeclaredShape and validates with NO findings — the positive witness of the projection contract (declare what you preserve, enumerate what you drop)." .

ex:ecProjectionMissingPreservationKind a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/projection-missing-preservation-kind.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The lang:ProjectionEmission names its target but declares no logic:preservationKind (sh:minCount 1 on lang:ProjectionEmissionDeclaredShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:MissingPreservationKind); lang:projectionTargetName is present. The four join-requiring projection failure classes (lang:UndeclaredUnsupportedConstruct, lang:UnrecordedEpistemicLoss, lang:ProjectionSilentDisambiguation, lang:ExactPreservationViolated) are native Rust gates (crates/validate structural_lint) tested in-crate, not SHACL, so their counter-examples (tests/counter-examples/projection-undeclared-unsupported.ttl, projection-unrecorded-epistemic-loss.ttl, projection-silent-disambiguation.ttl, projection-exact-preservation-violated.ttl) are exercised by the native lint tests." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Ingestion-stratum fixtures — the external-engine handoff. lang:UnattributedEngineClaim
# and lang:SilentPromotion are native Rust gates (crates/validate structural_lint,
# keyed on lang:interpretationEngine and lang:promotedReading) tested in-crate, not
# SHACL, so they have no example-conformance cell here; their counter-examples
# (tests/counter-examples/ingestion-unattributed-engine-claim.ttl and
# ingestion-silent-promotion.ttl) and the positive co-resident-readings fixture
# (tests/conformance-fixtures/ambiguity-saw-her-duck.ttl) are exercised by the native
# lint tests. lang:SilentDisambiguation (the co-resident-reading collapse) is likewise
# a native gate, noted with the meaning-stratum fixtures above.
# =========================================================================== #

# =========================================================================== #
# GMN dialect fixtures — the gmeow:gmn* graft's eight SHACL gates: canonical
# codepoints, the confusables blocklist, sigil-scoped glyph collisions, the
# nine-field envelope contract, the ring lattice, version overclaims,
# compaction provenance, and compaction overclaims. The five parser-tier failure classes
# (lang:GmnUncoveredTerm, lang:GmnNonCanonicalOrder, lang:GmnMalformedNumber,
# lang:GmnUndeclaredDialectVersion, lang:GmnNonDecodableGrammar) are the GMN
# parser/writer's own validator, not SHACL, so they have no cell here. The
# silent-collapse compaction counter-example
# (tests/counter-examples/gmn-compaction-silent-disambiguation.ttl) reuses the
# EXISTING bundle-wide lang:SilentDisambiguation discipline, a native Rust gate
# (crates/validate structural_lint) exercised by the native lint tests like
# projection-silent-disambiguation.ttl, so it likewise has no cell here.
# =========================================================================== #

ex:ecGmnScriptGlyphCanonical a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/gmn-script-glyph-canonical.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A @ℒ-scoped grapheme in gmeow:gmnScript with the canonical codepoint spelling \"U+2291\", its measured three-token cost, and a full lang:Denotation binding its operator form to canonical logic:subClassOf through gmeow:gmnDenotationGrapheme, plus two sigil-scoped glyphs lawfully sharing \"U+03BC\" (BOTH carry gmeow:gmnSigilScope, the exemption of lang:GmnGlyphCollisionShape) — satisfies the codepoint, confusable, collision, and grounding-direction gates and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecGmnEnvelopeComplete a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
