    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The gmeow:GmnEnvelope is generated by an activity typed gmeow:mentalProcessType gmeow:processExport (mentation) but declares no gmeow:gmnSecurityRing (the sh:sparql of lang:GmnExportRingBindingShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (lang:GmnUnringedExportCrossing). The class-qualified ring minimum of the derived gmeow:GmnEnvelope-shape ALSO fires on the same missing field (shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent, lang:GmnMissingEnvelopeField) — an honest double finding, since ring-absence is inherently covered by both the general envelope-contract gate and this export-specific binding gate; gmeow:expectedViolationCode pins the export-binding code this fixture exists to demonstrate." .

ex:ecGmnVersionOverclaim a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/gmn-version-overclaim.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The migration's carried correspondence claims logic:mnemomorphic true while the destination version's membership carries gmeow:versionScale gmeow:scaleMajor — a stronger-than-additive bump (the sh:sparql of lang:GmnVersionOverclaimShape) — so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (lang:GmnVersionOverclaim); the unit itself satisfies the translation-unit gates and the acceptance window is 1." .

ex:ecGmnCompactionWithoutProvenance a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
