# === Flagship acceptance manifest: the failure-range shape bites ============= #
#
# The shared cardinality wiring (an example, competency, producer, counter-example, and
# enforcing class, each exactly once) is now the shared gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape's job
# (shapes/gmeow-shapes.ttl), gated positively over examples/flagship-acceptance.ttl by
# `make validate` and by the native flagship cross-check (a missing required link drops the
# scenario from the coverage set). This slice's thin lang:FlagshipScenarioShape carries
# ONLY the failure-range sh:sparql, so the per-slice conformance cells exercise exactly
# that: a well-formed scenario conforms, and one whose enforcing class is not a
# lang:LangConformanceFailure subclass raises shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent.

ex:ecFlagshipCanonical a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/flagship-scenario-canonical.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A gmeow:FlagshipScenario binding all realizing artifacts (gmeow:demonstratedByExample, gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency, gmeow:demonstratedByProducer, gmeow:guardedByCounterExample) and naming an enforcing failure class that IS a lang:LangConformanceFailure subclass (lang:UnderspecifiedDenotation) passes the slice's thin lang:FlagshipScenarioShape failure-range sh:sparql, and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecFlagshipNonFailureClass a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/flagship-scenario-nonfailure-class.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a gmeow:FlagshipScenario whose gmeow:enforcesFailureClass names lang:Grammar — a real class that is NOT a lang:LangConformanceFailure subclass (the failure-range sh:sparql of the slice's thin lang:FlagshipScenarioShape). That constraint fires, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (lang:UnwiredFlagshipScenario) — the enforcing failure class is checked by value." .
